  "authored_scope": "Supported: the original 2x2, 1xN and Nx1 (N = 2..4) layouts. Synthetic extensions add 1x5, 5x1, 1x6, 6x1, 2x3 and 3x2 layouts, where the 30-cell limit allows them. Default panel sides are 4..10, and explicit sides of 3..28 are accepted when they fit. Height and width may differ. Both chain axes are supported for each layout where feasible. Shapes come from up to eight colours, which may repeat. Middle panels may be straight bars with entry == exit, which reproduces the train-3 situation: repeated contacts plus full-grid-line distractors in 1xN vertical and Nx1 horizontal scenes. Not supported: other background or divider colours, ragged or unequal panels, multi-cell contacts, shapes that touch the cross-axis edges, and branching or ambiguous chains. 1x5 and 1x6 layouts only allow horizontal chains, and 5x1 and 6x1 only vertical ones, because of the 30-cell bound.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Background 7 is strictly the most frequent input colour.",
    "Shape colours never equal 6 or 7.",
    "Every shape-colour full grid line count is strictly less than the number of divider lines.",
    "Every contact is a single interior cell on a chain-axis edge. Shapes never touch the cross-axis edges.",
    "Exactly one panel has no entry contact and exactly one has no exit contact.",
    "Exactly one ordering of the panels satisfies the chain rule (checked by exhaustive search, n <= 6).",
    "When several remaining panels share the matching entry, the true successor is the earliest in reading order. This is the train-3 tie situation, and bars are only placed where it holds.",
    "Bar panels are never adjacent in the chain, because adjacent bars would share a column and make the order ambiguous.",
    "An aligned layout (Nx1 vertical or 1xN horizontal) never uses the identity order.",
    "Input and output dimensions stay within 30."
